# User-facing copy (law)

Read skill **forja-user-facing-copy** when editing manifests, UI strings, pack blurbs, feature docs, or changelog wording users read.

**Law:** Product strings describe **what it does now** — not migrations, architecture, or history.

| Forbidden in user-facing strings | |
|----------------------------------|--|
| “only / no longer / formerly / separate packs” | |
| Architecture lectures (`host-owned`, `kit protocol`, …) | |
| Stale provider/feature lists after code dropped them | |
| Contrastive copy pitched at users (`Not X — Y`) | |

When behavior changes: read live UI → rewrite every stale string → grep ids across packs/app/web/features/changelog.

**Sniff:** would a normal user care? If it’s only for a developer’s refactor, delete it from the product string.
